{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And Elohim saw all that He had made</b> etc. — even the evil inclination." "<b>And behold, it was very good.</b> For were it not for the evil inclination, a man would not marry a wife nor beget sons, and it would follow that the world does not endure. On the sixth day, כי טוב was said twice — once for the creation of the beasts and once for the creation of man." "<b>The sixth day.</b> The day that is specified and known among the other days, for on it alone all the work of creation was completed — which was not so on the other days. And thus it is written: ״כי ששת ימים עשה ה׳ את השמים ואת הארץ את הים״ etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:20:17.313472043Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}